  <static seed="142" source="Library/Michigan/Chap3Sec1/Q11.pg">
    <statement><p>Find the derivative of 
<m>\displaystyle{f(x)=\frac{1}{x^{15}} }</m>.</p>
<p><m>f'(x) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>-1\cdot 15x^{-1\cdot \left(15+1\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x) = \frac{1}{x^{15}} = x^{-15}</m>, so

<me>f'(x) = -15 x^{-15 - 1} = -15 x^{-16}.</me>



</solution>
